#!/bin/sh
# The `docker` the harness resolves through PATH when farm/env.py has put this
# directory first.  All logic lives in farm/teardown.py; this wrapper's one job
# is to guarantee the real docker runs exactly once whatever happens to python.
#
# Contract with teardown.py: it exits 97 ONLY if it failed before reaching
# execv, i.e. the real command has not run -- so we run it.  Any other exit
# code came from the real docker after execv and is propagated unchanged; a
# second run would turn one `docker stop` into two.
REAL="${FARM_REAL_DOCKER:-/usr/bin/docker}"
HERE="$(dirname "$0")"
if command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  python3 "$HERE/../teardown.py" "$@"
  rc=$?
  [ "$rc" -eq 97 ] || exit "$rc"
fi
exec "$REAL" "$@"
